<section class="how-section" id="how">
  <div class="s-label reveal">How It Works</div>
  <h2 class="s-title reveal stagger-1">Five Steps to a Sweater<br><em>That Fits Your Body</em></h2>
  <p class="s-body reveal stagger-2">You don't need to redesign anything from scratch. You just need to know where to look, what to fix, and how to do it without breaking the pattern.</p>
  <div class="steps-list">
    <div class="step-item reveal"><div class="step-num">01</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-icon">📏</div><div class="step-title">Find Your Starting Point</div><div class="step-desc">You measure your body, compare it to the pattern schematic, and pick the best base size. No more guessing. You know exactly where you're starting before you crochet a single stitch.</div><div class="step-includes">Includes: Fit First Blueprint + Choose Your Base Size Calculator</div></div></div>
    <div class="step-item reveal"><div class="step-num">02</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-icon">🔍</div><div class="step-title">Isolate the Problem Zones</div><div class="step-desc">Not everything needs to change. You pinpoint the exact sections that don't match your body — bust, waist, hips, sleeves — and leave the rest alone. Targeted. Precise. No tent shapes.</div><div class="step-includes">Includes: Sectional Resizing Toolkit</div></div></div>
    <div class="step-item reveal"><div class="step-num">03</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-icon">🧮</div><div class="step-title">Decode Your Gauge</div><div class="step-desc">This is where most projects go wrong before they even begin. You learn to measure both stitch and row gauge correctly, so your garment comes out the right width and the right length, every time.</div><div class="step-includes">Includes: The Gauge De-Coder</div></div></div>
    <div class="step-item reveal"><div class="step-num">04</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-icon">✂️</div><div class="step-title">Adjust Without Breaking the Design</div><div class="step-desc">You add or remove stitches in the right multiples, so cables stay centered and lace stays seamless. The pattern looks exactly as the designer intended — just sized for your body.</div><div class="step-includes">Includes: The Pattern Integrity Shield</div></div></div>
    <div class="step-item reveal"><div class="step-num">05</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-icon">👗</div><div class="step-title">Grade Between Sizes Like a Pro</div><div class="step-desc">Medium shoulders. XL bust. No problem. You blend sizes across different sections so the garment fits your actual shape — not a proportional average that doesn't exist in real life.</div><div class="step-includes">Includes: Sectional Resizing Toolkit + Construction-Type Cheat Sheets</div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
